    "Built 19 Oct 2026 (Indices clip 4) from 108.15 with 108.13's words: the question read top then bottom; why nothing cancels yet (the powers differ; only a factor of the whole top and bottom cancels — a written drop-down); the plan as maths (3^n(□)/3^n(△) = □/△); split every power — Add power in reverse, a^{x+k} = a^x × a^k — each of the four terms lit as it is named; a split is always a times (the common mistake 3^n + 3, at the step); every term has 3^n, take it out top and bottom; 3^n multiplies the whole top and bottom, so it cancels; only numbers left — a negative power is one over (3 − 1/9)/(1/3 − 9), then the calculator: 26/9 over −26/3; times its flip 26/9 × (−3/26); = −1/3, boxed. One expression line by line, no headings, no step numbers, no Watch out."
